          "title": "You'll want to know: ಮಸಿ",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "ಮಸಿ — masi — \"soot\"."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "ಹಳೆಯ ಬಸ್ಸಿನ ಹೊಗೆಯಿಂದ ಗೋಡೆಗೆ ಮಸಿ ಹಿಡಿಯಿತು. haḷeya bassina hogeyinda gōḍege masi hiḍiyitu. The smoke of an old bus left soot on the wall."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "In older Kannada it was also ink."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 2,
          "type": "etymology",
          "title": "The word, taken apart",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "ಮಸಿ (masi) is native Dravidian: DEDR 5101 lists Kannada masi, \"soot, lampblack, ink\", beside Tamil mai. Sanskrit maṣi, masi, \"lampblack, ink\", was itself taken from Dravidian, as Turner notes (CDIAL 9920)."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 3,
          "type": "notice",
          "title": "What you've built",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "One more word for getting around."
